{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning","id":1527146,"title":"Can Cain die by sun tanning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-21T03:52:14-08:00","id":1527146,"title":"Can Cain die by sun tanning?","content":"I have been reading up on how the Ravnos Antediluvian was only killed after a seriously long huge battle, hit by neutron bombs and only finished off with concentrated sunlight.<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder... If an Antediluvian is so tough to kill... Needing to be seriously weaken first AND <b>concentrated</b> sunlight... Then just how tough is the original vampire, Cain?<br /> <br /> Can (a healthy) Cain go sun bathing in full summer sunlight for a whole day?<br /> <br /> Would he turn to ash? Or would he just get a tan and a terrible thirst?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T04:00:05-08:00","id":1527147,"title":"","content":"I imagine not. Even ignoring powers that would make it a non-issue, I doubt an angel would put a curse that would kill him when God wanted Caine to repent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T04:04:46-08:00","id":1527148,"title":"","content":"I think the best method to model Caine would be to use the rules for Abyssal Exalted operating in sunlight. It's a dice modifier rather than direct damage. As the curse weakened with each generation, sunlight became more detrimental to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T05:54:44-08:00","id":1527149,"title":"","content":"Look, I believe he could if you consider what we know, the antediluvian of the Ravnos had such a high level of Fortitude that he resisted three neutron bombs, or atomic bombs, I don't know, it's true that he died in the sun afterwards, but you can see he was very resistant, based on this presumption I believe that Cain, being older and more experienced, would be capable of doing the same if not more, whether with fortitude or another method, although I think he would have no reason to To do so, I mean, as a vampire his dead body cannot tan even though it survives the sun aside from that he must still feel tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T06:04:10-08:00","id":1527150,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the Ravnos ante also one of the Yama Kings of the Thousand Hells (Ravana, I believe)? That could explain his superior resistance (in addition to Fortitude 10)...<br /> <br /> Also, (assuming he is real at all) if Caine could be destroyed by sunlight, wouldn't that go against the purpose of his curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T06:32:26-08:00","id":1527151,"title":"","content":"Most likely he would burn in agony, but not actually be destroyed. At least that would be my interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T06:55:56-08:00","id":1527153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527150#post1527150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Ravnos ante also one of the Yama Kings of the Thousand Hells (Ravana, I believe)? That could explain his superior resistance (in addition to Fortitude 10)...<br /> <br /> Also, (assuming he is real at all) if Caine could be destroyed by sunlight, wouldn't that go against the purpose of his curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was actually his child Ravana that became a Yama King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T07:16:58-08:00","id":1527156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527153#post1527153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was actually his child Ravana that became a Yama King.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that confirmed somewhere? Because <i>Time of the Thin-Blooded </i>(in the &quot;this is the truth&quot; part of the Appendix) says he takes the form of Ravana. <i>The Thousand Hells </i>doesn't explain much, but that's an older book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T07:47:35-08:00","id":1527158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning#post1527146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can (a healthy) Cain go sun bathing in full summer sunlight for a whole day?<br /> <br /> Would he turn to ash? Or would he just get a tan and a terrible thirst?</div> </div> </div> </div>Complicated question<br /> Depending of many factors<br /> <br /> Raphael's - the driver of the Sun, ward of the East - curse according the Book of Nod was &quot;For as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always&quot;<br /> It is a bit of the extension of Michael's - General of Heaven, wielder of the holy Flame - curse &quot;For as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> When it come to those ancient and powerful curses, wording is important - and you can notice, neither of the archangel's curse actually say the Sun or the Fire will destroy them - well no more than any other human, I mean set someone on fire and they will die a very painfull death and consant sunlight could be deadly too<br /> <br /> It is not important what system or relegion or setting you use, be it Ra, Helios, or Raphael Caine have the sevenfold curse &quot;Whoever kills Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.\u201d - and no Celestine, Elohim or sungod is fool enough to risk <i>that </i><br /> (And in WoD the Sun is perfectly capable to withold it powers, good example the Serpentis power &quot;Pact with Ra&quot; that calls upon the debt incurred when Sutek defended <i>Ra</i> against the monstrous serpent Apep.. and the Setite who uses this power until the next sunrise will be utterly unaffected by sunlight and daytime...)<br /> <br /> But I guess the more important, if we stay purely on Vampire ground?<br /> The Curses were punishments meted out specifically to Caine so that Caine would <b><i>suffer</i></b><br /> Sure, they effect his descendants but that is more like &quot;collateral damage&quot; so with Fortitude they can begin to withstand the curse that wasn't even really <i>meant</i> for them<br /> But when it comes to Caine? No amount of Fortitude will save him from the Curse!<br /> Caine will always suffer the bane of his curse at its original strength until he truly repents or the world truly ends. Whichever comes first.<br /> And Caine knows perfectly well why God <b><i>won't let him die</i></b> - because he won't apologize for killing Abel.<br /> <br /> So Caine would burn, scream, he could tear his own burning flesh of, he could do whatever he want, from dawn till dusk, he will be in unimaginable agony <i>but he wont die</i>.<br /> He will never die unless God Almighty allows it - and by Nahum 1:2-15 &quot;The Lord is a jealous God, filled with vengeance and rage!&quot; So don't expect any mercy from Above...<br /> The Sun don't technically have to withold its power, because the sevenfold curse triggers only when Caine dies<br /> <br /> (But it is fun to toy with the idea, solar eclipses and Little Ice Ages\u200b are the times when Caine tried to end his suffering, the Sun got weakened, but God not let him die)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T07:58:13-08:00","id":1527159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527156#post1527156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that confirmed somewhere? Because <i>Time of the Thin-Blooded </i>(in the &quot;this is the truth&quot; part of the Appendix) says he takes the form of Ravana. <i>The Thousand Hells </i>doesn't explain much, but that's an older book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clanbook: Ravnos Revised details how Ravana thrown in his lot with demons and abandoned his master Zapathasura, and tried tempting his Sire into infernalism.<br /> Ravana was said to bargain with true demons for power even greater than Zapathasura before disappearing<br /> Around this time the Yama King known as Ravana apeard and rose to power (tho' this is a bit harder to confirm, since the &quot;history&quot; regarding the the Yama Kings are murky at best. For example The Kitsune and the Nuwisha both claim Hanuman who infiltrated the Yama King's Hell was one of their own, - though the legends suggest that Hanuman was a monkey and we actually have a Hsien (or Shinma), the &quot;little gods&quot; of the Middle Kingdom legend about a Hanuman who was a Hsien - With masterful stealth, Hanuman infiltrated Lanka and, using Gifts given to him <i>specifically</i> to punish Ravana, he engulfed the whole island in cleansing fire and ruined Lanka)<br /> 1000 Hells, Hengeyokai and Land of Eight Million Dreams a bit hard to navigate when it comes to &quot;facts&quot;, but from several supplements it is more of deductable than written fact, the Yama King Ravna is the Ravnos Ravana who &quot;ascended&quot; (descended) in to Yomi and carved out a Hell of his own.<br /> Ravana, the Yama King's descirption eerly match the Ravnos one actually...<br /> Besides, a vampire becoming a Demon is not unheard of, Mary the Black and Nergal/Huitzilopochtli both managed to become a Demon<br /> Mikaboshi, lord of the Wicked City is another Yama King was a mortal; he was originally a Japanese scholar and fang shih who was invited by the Chinese court to be an advisor. Unfortunately, he was consumed by a lust for power, and turned to infernalism. He created many architectural configurations to develop and focus corrupted chi through the Yin world to fuel his magics, but was eventually found out, forcing him to flee into the spirit worlds permanently and became a Yama King<br /> So if a mortal could have done it with infernalism and 4th Generation Ravnos easly could have done the same (just way earlier)<br /> <br /> True, there is not 100% confirmed Ravan the Ravnos is Ravana the Yama King, I must admit, but I would say, according those supplements?<br /> 99% he is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> True, Night of Prophecies said: &quot;Psychics, madmen, and anyone even vaguely touched by the supernatural felt on edge or suffered visions and nightmares. The nightmares usually featured the Demon-King Ravana&quot; - but those are just nightmares, not the &quot;real deal&quot;<br /> <br /> But for me it is a good excuse, so when I use the Week of Nightmares, who rampaged its not Zapatashura usually<br /> Not a Ravnos Antediluvian either<br /> But Ravana, Yama King of the realm know as Lanka, the Demon City of the Rakshas who was presided over the souls of the violent.<br /> But things changed and Lanka became a ruined &quot;dying&quot; hell; the domain of the lord of the Rakshasa, Ravana was assulted and almost destroyed. Ravana has fallen into deeper apathy and depression since his defeat by Hanuman, abandoning the city mostly to its own devices. Hanuman was a Kitsune (or a monkey... tales are a bit blurry)<br /> After Hanuman danced thrugh Lanka burning it with rightous fire, Ravana lost much of his powerbase... in the eyes of the other Yama Kings, he was out of the game for the Throne of the Demon Emperor. But Ravana wasn't destroyed and had his schemes. Mostly involving nuclear fire and tainted chi...<br /> Back to the Week of Nightmares!<br /> In my stories the Yama King was the one who &quot;awoke&quot;/returned, weakened state, forced back to his original undead body and went on a rampage and the three Bodhisattvas arrived, since the Kuei-.jin's first and foremost enemies are not the Ravnos, but the Yama Kings - true, the Ravnos, the indian Tzimisce and the Kuei-jin hate each other with passion, that hate is because the shared territory; the Kuei-jin vs Yama King thing is far more serious.<br /> <br /> This lines nicely with the description in time of thin blood after the nukes:<br /> &quot;A vaguely human figure staggered toward Tieh Ju through the rain. She guessed it might be male but could not be sure. Flakes of black ash covered the remains of its naked, shriveled body. One arm hung as a stump of tattered meat. Hallucinations of pain radiated from it, like the vibrating, inner light of migraine. It had survived the wrath of three Bodhisattvas and a bath of nuclear fire. Tieh Ju knew that, even weakened as it was, she could not fight it. If she tried, it would replenish its strength on her chi. Although the thing had no eyes, only sockets oozing black blood, it turned to face the pair. Its fanged jaws worked, and it rasped out, &quot;Blood. Feed. Hunger.&quot; It spoke Sanskrit, the ancient tongue of India.&quot;<br /> <br /> And at the end, the Sun destroyed his body, not only because he was a vampire once, but back in the third (or fourth can't remember) Age the Yama Kings made a little mistake, when summoned several other suns and almost burnt the planet, it needed a shamed celestial dragon, a hero named Yi, who arrowed down the False Suns and in some stories a flood, to make things right<br /> And after this little incident, the August Personage of Jade added the curse of the Sun to the weekneses of the Kuei-jin, because most of them helped the Yama Kings and punsihed his wayward jailors too...<br /> Anyhow, these things comes together nicely, Ravana returned, then lost and ened up destroyed; he failed to absorb the chi of thousands murdered in Bangladesh and the tainted nuclear fires power to return to power, to be powerfull Yama King and died.<br /> <br /> When I use Zapathasura, he tricked the world by the ultimate illusion, used Chimerstry and changed reality, used his power to make the world think he had died to be either escape the Jyhad or to be free from the Gods and his task (the story goes, the gods took the soul of the man most grievously wronged by the asuratizayya and gave him new life, making him a monster so that he and his descendants might hunt the asuratizayya. Though many of the gods bestowed him with great gifts to further his cause, not all of them agreed to creating another dark force in the world. Three placed curses upon the man so that he should fear falling into temptation as the siddhittizaya had, and so the man would forever be threatened by the touch of fire and sunlight, and would also know an eternity of physical and spiritual hunger just as the creatures he hunted. Named Zapathasura, or &quot;accursed demon&quot;, he was then sent out to drive the infernal hordes from the world.)\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T10:11:37-08:00","id":1527171,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that one of the scenarios of <u>Gehenna</u> concludes with a little teaser that involves someone who is all but explicitly stated to be Caine pulling himself out of the dust after the end of the world as we know it, and angrily screaming up at Heaven for not allowing him to just *die* already.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that Caine would probably have enough Fortitude to at least mostly-resist the damage caused by sunlight. The vampiric Disciplines come from the power of the Curse, at least in part, but they weren't exactly part of the plan, either, so I wouldn't rule that Caine is uniquely vulnerable. How exactly you'd want to run that would be up to you. You could just decide what level of vulnerability/resistance Caine has and play accordingly, or you could try to calculate realistically how well a character with 10 or 11 dots in Fortitude could soak sunlight.<br /> <br /> And if Caine can't soak with Fortitude, then he's gonna burn. The question is what the ultimate outcome will be. I do agree that allowing Caine to be ended by sunlight creates a bit of a flaw if you have a version that might be inclined to end his own existence, so I probably wouldn't make that an option. If Caine is going to be *killed* then it requires an act of murder on the part of his killer, in my opinion, who would then suffer the Sevenfold Curse (I also wouldn't want Caine dying by sunlight to effectively turn said Curse loose on Helios, either).<br /> <br /> So if you don't want sunlight as a possible permanent end for the First Vampire, but you don't want him to be immune either, then the best remaining options seem to be:<br /> <br /> a) He just doesn't stop burning. It's painful, probably does a lot of damage that he'll need to recover from eventually, but Caine will not suffer Final Death no matter what due to sunlight.<br /> <br /> (For people into B-movies, the straight-to-video sequel for Dracula 2000 might provide an example of what this could look like.)<br /> <br /> b) Caine is a bit like ol' Prometheus. Caine is absolutely capable of burning down to nothing but ash in sunlight. But come evening, Caine will reform and reawaken. If the ashes are scattered, he'll rise out of the earth itself where the faintest trace of his remains might have landed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:39:13-08:00","id":1527184,"title":"","content":"Myself if we go by the lore at all is that Cain would feel intense pain and want to hide from the sun, but I don't think it would cause him final death as God wouldn't allow it to happen until he felt the time was right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T18:41:09-08:00","id":1527217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527184#post1527184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself if we go by the lore at all is that Cain would feel intense pain and want to hide from the sun, but I don't think it would cause him final death as God wouldn't allow it to happen until he felt the time was right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's this tiny problem that God may be dead. The Holy Seals based on His will are failing left and right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T23:12:50-08:00","id":1527224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527217#post1527217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but that's this tiny problem that God may be dead. The Holy Seals based on His will are failing left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a funny angle too!<br /> If you take the Book of Nod &quot;version&quot;, the &quot;vampiric curses&quot; came from the Archangels, not God - only the Sevenfold Curse was handed out by God<br /> So maaaaaybe they could hold even without God?<br /> (Or with a Mage splash, the divine spark that allows them to Awake is a God-fregment and actually Humanity and the concensus responsible for upholding the Curses... everyone knows vampires are affected by sunlight, stake, etc... so the collective belief make it so)<br /> <br /> Sprinkle a little Demon:the Fallen in the mix and you get an interesting situation, because Lucifer and Michael after the last battle of Genhinnom that resulted in Heaven's victory and the banishment of the Fallen to the Abyss, before the night of banishment had a little... talk. Michael went to the chained Lucifer and what they talked about is unknown, but afterwards he threw away his sword and left it within Creation (interestingly, later Michael tutored the Salubri Samiel and the whole tradition to take up and use an Angel's celestial name begun, making the Salubri warriors Michael little private undead army...) <br /> Similar happened with Gabriel, at the defense of Shamayim, where he fought and later refused an order of God himself to retreat from the battlefield, in order to protect a mortal woman. At the end of the battle, Gabriel had vanished and did not appear again during the course of the war. Some Demons believe that Gabriel chose to fall instead of abandoning his love. If this is the case, he was not banished into the Abyss <br /> In Michhael case, since he handed out the fire-curse it is amusing to think, after his more-or-less desertation (well he just threw away his sword... so could remain loyal to Haven) Michael's curse also could lessened if not outright possibly gone<br /> Gabriel is another can of worms, because he not handed out a curse but promised Caine salvation if he ever seeks to repent. Gabriel opened the way to all Kindred to achieve Golconda and earn individual salvation... with him deserting, that promise could be gone and Golconda is a lie - or the opposite, since Gabriel went off the map, as a rebelious Archangel the state of Golconda could be more possible than ever?<br /> On the other hand, in the Erciyes Fragments, Gabriel is the third Archangel to appear before Caine, referred to as &quot;Dread Gabriel, by whose hands Gomorrha was destroyed&quot;. After his offer of forgiveness is refused, Gabriel curses Caine with hunger for blood, sets him apart from the living and spreads the seeds of rebellion into his progeny, fulfilling a role that is traditionally held by Uriel.<br /> If we take the Erciyes Fragments rute, a rebelious Gabriel is a terrifyng thought - and if that version went off the map, the blood drinking curse gains an even darker twist....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T03:11:30-08:00","id":1527226,"title":"","content":"In my Headcanon, God allowed supernatural creatures to exist and even made some, just as a way to send things towards the apocalypse and test humanity to see if they are worthy or is it better to recreate everything again, the morning star's betrayal was for this purpose and not even the fallen imagine it, Cain's curse is just an instrument for this chaos to happen and Malkav's madness is because he had a glimpse of the truth and that is why he allowed all this mess to happen. This has nothing to do with the conversation, I just saw the topic unfold and felt like writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T03:22:28-08:00","id":1527227,"title":"","content":"In my head cannon Cappadocius succeeded and now sits on the throne of Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T09:28:24-08:00","id":1527245,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon, Set walks under the Sun by Cain with a troupe of Setites with VDA20 Serpentis 3 and Fortitude 6+. Cain's burning and suffering, while Set and followers are chilling because they're soaking the Sun's 3 levels of damage with 6+ Fortitude dice on a difficulty of 5 (because VDA20 reduces all soaking difficulties to 5, even though it doesn't let use Stamina to soak sunlight and fire, hence the need of Fortitude), averaging no damage.<br /> Cain's got Fortitude 12, but assuming he has no anti-Sun custom powers (which he might totally have), if he takes the Sun's rays full on (diff.9 to soak), he's still taking damage each turn, but without being able to die.<br /> <br /> Then every Cappadocian of any generation with VDA20 Corpse in the Monster 5 passes by and they're chilling even more than the Setites. Yes, Cappadocius might have actually managed to do something, unbeknownst to all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T22:21:26-08:00","id":1527286,"title":"","content":"It'd give him a really deep burn and allow him to utilize the Satsui no Hadou. But I may be thinking of something else and sun tanning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:08:27-07:00","id":1536958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning#post1527146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been reading up on how the Ravnos Antediluvian was only killed after a seriously long huge battle, hit by neutron bombs and only finished off with concentrated sunlight.<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder... If an Antediluvian is so tough to kill... Needing to be seriously weaken first AND <b>concentrated</b> sunlight... Then just how tough is the original vampire, Cain?<br /> <br /> Can (a healthy) Cain go sun bathing in full summer sunlight for a whole day?<br /> <br /> Would he turn to ash? Or would he just get a tan and a terrible thirst?</div> </div> </div> </div>He will probably never die due to the sun, due to God's curse. He would probably suffer greatly, but not die. The whole reason for his curse is to forget his pride, and repent. Until he does so, he will live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:14:25-07:00","id":1536959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527146-can-cain-die-by-sun-tanning?p=1527245#post1527245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my headcanon, Set walks under the Sun by Cain with a troupe of Setites with VDA20 Serpentis 3 and Fortitude 6+. Cain's burning and suffering, while Set and followers are chilling because they're soaking the Sun's 3 levels of damage with 6+ Fortitude dice on a difficulty of 5 (because VDA20 reduces all soaking difficulties to 5, even though it doesn't let use Stamina to soak sunlight and fire, hence the need of Fortitude), averaging no damage.<br /> Cain's got Fortitude 12, but assuming he has no anti-Sun custom powers (which he might totally have), if he takes the Sun's rays full on (diff.9 to soak), he's still taking damage each turn, but without being able to die.<br /> <br /> Then every Cappadocian of any generation with VDA20 Corpse in the Monster 5 passes by and they're chilling even more than the Setites. Yes, Cappadocius might have actually managed to do something, unbeknownst to all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot the part where Caine was an awakened Mage before being cursed, awakened by Lilith's ritual and blood, and can invent new Disciplines on the spot. Any Discipline that any Clan has, or has even thought of, he can do, instantaneously. He's probably been walking in the sun for hundreds of thousands of years, albeit not like a normal human for 12+ hours. He's the literal OG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}